  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework's performance and transferability were evaluated using data from a single city, Rotterdam.",
      "what": "The researchers developed Q-Net, a state-space queue estimation framework that integrates aggregated vehicle counts from loop detectors with segment-wise average speed measurements from floating car data. Tested on urban main roads in Rotterdam, Netherlands, the model uses an AI-augmented Kalman filter to learn time-varying gain dynamics and groups speed measurements into fixed-size local groups to keep parameters independent of road section length.",
      "why": "It enables accurate, real-time queue length estimation on signalized intersections using existing, privacy-preserving data sources, eliminating the need for expensive physical sensing infrastructure like cameras or radar."
